IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc32-related-1.l4 -- the related provisions of amending Acts, 1991 to 2015, from the end of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46
-- (lines 19056-19167 of the text: 1991, c. 43, s. 10; 2004, c. 12, ss. 22 and 23; 2009, c. 29, s. 5; 2011, c. 2, s. 7; 2012, c. 1, ss. 163 and 165; 2015, c. 13, ss. 37 to 44; 2015, c. 20, s. 28).
-- Part ccc32, layer 1. Imports the keel's `ccc-core` (Party, Provision of the Code) and `daydate` (dates are `Date day month year`).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30). It is not the official text,
-- and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
--
-- NAMING. A provision of an amending Act is labelled as the text headers it: year, chapter, section (`2015 c 13 s 44 ...`). That cannot collide with a Code
-- section label (`s 44 ...`) another part encodes. Every top-level name, type and constructor begins with the label of its provision.
--
-- HOW A RESULT READS (details: NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (ccc32)"). Every decision answers a MAYBE BOOLEAN.
--   JUST TRUE    the facts bring the case within the provision, on its own words;
--   JUST FALSE   the text says no in its own words: an "only", a flat negative, an "until", a period fixed in the text, a failed "if" within the provision (a marginal reading);
--   NOTHING      not covered: the grant is limited by its own wording and the case falls outside the limit, the text is silent, or it points outside the sources.
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
--
-- THE DAYS THE TEXT LEAVES TO COMMENCEMENT ("the day on which section 12 of this Act comes into force") ARE INPUTS: none of those days is in the sources.
-- A provision that is a duty of an official is encoded for what it means to the person (what is continued, deemed or limited) and, where it has a named duty-bearer and a period, as a regulative rule as well.

§ `1991, c. 43, s. 10 -- Lieutenant Governor warrants or orders remain in force`

-- (1) Any order for detention made under section 614, 615 or 617 of the Code or section 200 or 201 of the National Defence Act, as those sections read immediately before 1991, c. 43 ss. 3 or 18 came into force,
-- continues in force until an order is made by a court or Review Board under section 672.54.
-- src:19057 | Lieutenant Governor warrants or orders remain in force
-- src:19058 | 10 (1) Any order for detention of an accused or accused person made under section 614, 615 or 617 of the Criminal Code or section 200 or 201 of the National Defence Act, as those sections read immediately before the coming into force of section 3 or 18 of this Act, shall continue in force until an order is made by a court or Review Board under section 672.54 of the Criminal Code.
@ref 1991, c. 43, s. 10(1) (src:19057-19058)
DECLARE `1991 c 43 s 10(1) kind of order for detention` IS ONE OF
    `1991 c 43 s 10(1) an order under section 614 of the Criminal Code`
    `1991 c 43 s 10(1) an order under section 615 of the Criminal Code`
    `1991 c 43 s 10(1) an order under section 617 of the Criminal Code`
    `1991 c 43 s 10(1) an order under section 200 of the National Defence Act`
    `1991 c 43 s 10(1) an order under section 201 of the National Defence Act`
    `1991 c 43 s 10(1) an order of another kind`

@ref 1991, c. 43, s. 10(1) (src:19057-19058)
GIVEN kind IS A `1991 c 43 s 10(1) kind of order for detention`
      `the order was made under that section as it read immediately before the coming into force of section 3 or 18 of 1991, c. 43` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an order has been made by a court or Review Board under section 672.54` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`1991 c 43 s 10(1) the order for detention continues in force` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF kind EQUALS `1991 c 43 s 10(1) an order of another kind` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "made under section 614, 615 or 617 of the Criminal Code or section 200 or 201 of the National Defence Act"
        IF NOT `the order was made under that section as it read immediately before the coming into force of section 3 or 18 of 1991, c. 43` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as those sections read immediately before the coming into force of section 3 or 18 of this Act"
        IF `an order has been made by a court or Review Board under section 672.54` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall continue in force until an order is made by a court or Review Board under section 672.54 of the Criminal Code"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (2) The Review Board of a province shall, within twelve months after the coming into force of this section, review the case of every person detained in custody in the province by virtue of an order of detention referred to in (1).
-- The duty-bearer is the core party `a Review Board`; the period is twelve MONTHS, so a trace of this rule counts time in months (WITHIN 12).
-- src:19059 | Review of inmates held in custody on lieutenant governor warrants or orders
-- src:19060 | (2) The Review Board of a province shall, within twelve months after the coming into force of this section, review the case of every person detained in custody in the province by virtue of an order of detention referred to in subsection (1).
@ref 1991, c. 43, s. 10(2) (src:19059-19060)
DECLARE `1991 c 43 s 10(2) act` IS ONE OF
    `1991 c 43 s 10(2) review the case of a person detained in custody by virtue of an order of detention referred to in subsection (1)`

@ref 1991, c. 43, s. 10(2) (src:19059-19060)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `1991 c 43 s 10(2) act`
`1991 c 43 s 10(2) the Review Board must review the case` MEANS
    PARTY `a Review Board`
    MUST `1991 c 43 s 10(2) review the case of a person detained in custody by virtue of an order of detention referred to in subsection (1)`
    WITHIN 12
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `a Review Board` BECAUSE "the case of a person detained under an order referred to in subsection 10(1) was not reviewed within twelve months after the coming into force of section 10"

-- The same period as a decision: the review was within twelve months after the coming into force (the day itself to the same day twelve months on).
@ref 1991, c. 43, s. 10(2) (src:19059-19060)
GIVEN `the day on which section 10 of 1991, c. 43 came into force` IS A DATE
      `the day the Review Board reviewed the case` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`1991 c 43 s 10(2) the review was within twelve months after the coming into force` MEANS
    IF `the day the Review Board reviewed the case` AT LEAST `the day on which section 10 of 1991, c. 43 came into force`
       AND `the day the Review Board reviewed the case` AT MOST (`add months` `the day on which section 10 of 1991, c. 43 came into force` 12)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within twelve months after the coming into force of this section"

-- (3) Sections 672.5 to 672.85 apply, with such modifications as the circumstances require, to a review under (2) as if (a) it were a review of a disposition conducted under 672.81 and (b) the LG's warrant were a disposition under 672.54.
-- src:19061 | Application of sections 672.5 to 672.85 to reviews under subsection (2)
-- src:19062 | (3) Sections 672.5 to 672.85 of the Criminal Code apply, with such modifications as the circumstances require, to a review under subsection (2) as if
-- src:19063 | (a) the review were a review of a disposition conducted pursuant to section 672.81 of that Act; and
-- src:19064 | (b) the warrant issued by the lieutenant governor pursuant to which the person is being detained in custody were a disposition made under section 672.54 of that Act.
@ref 1991, c. 43, s. 10(3) (src:19061-19064)
GIVEN `the section of the Code` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the proceeding is a review under subsection 10(2) of 1991, c. 43` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`1991 c 43 s 10(3) the section applies, with such modifications as the circumstances require, to the review` MEANS
    IF `the proceeding is a review under subsection 10(2) of 1991, c. 43`
       AND `the section of the Code`'s `section` AT LEAST 672.5
       AND `the section of the Code`'s `section` AT MOST 672.85
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Sections 672.5 to 672.85 of the Criminal Code apply, with such modifications as the circumstances require, to a review under subsection (2)"

@ref 1991, c. 43, s. 10(3)(a) (src:19063)
GIVEN `the proceeding is a review under subsection 10(2) of 1991, c. 43` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`1991 c 43 s 10(3)(a) the review is treated as a review of a disposition conducted under section 672.81` MEANS
    IF `the proceeding is a review under subsection 10(2) of 1991, c. 43`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to a review under subsection (2) as if"

@ref 1991, c. 43, s. 10(3)(b) (src:19064)
GIVEN `the proceeding is a review under subsection 10(2) of 1991, c. 43` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the warrant is the warrant issued by the lieutenant governor pursuant to which the person is being detained in custody` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`1991 c 43 s 10(3)(b) the warrant is treated as a disposition made under section 672.54` MEANS
    IF `the proceeding is a review under subsection 10(2) of 1991, c. 43` AND `the warrant is the warrant issued by the lieutenant governor pursuant to which the person is being detained in custody`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the warrant issued by the lieutenant governor pursuant to which the person is being detained in custody were a disposition made under section 672.54 of that Act"

-- (3)(c) and (d), and (4) to (7), are shown repealed by the text: carried as quotations of what the text shows.
-- src:19065 | (c) and (d) [Repealed, 2005, c. 22, s. 43]
-- src:19066 | (4) to (7) [Repealed, 2005, c. 22, s. 43]
