`1991 c 43 s 10(4) to (7) as the text shows them` MEANS "[Repealed, 2005, c. 22, s. 43]"

§ `2004, c. 12, ss. 22 and 23 -- how two references in 2001, c. 32, s. 82 are read`

-- 22 For greater certainty, section 82 of 2001, c. 32 is to be read in accordance with (a) to (c). A rule of reading over a small typed representation of the reference.
-- src:19069 | Interpretation of 2001, c. 32, ss. 82(1), (2) and (4)
-- src:19070 | 22 For greater certainty, section 82 of An Act to amend the Criminal Code (organized crime and law enforcement) and to make consequential amendments to other Acts (“the Act”), chapter 32 of the Statutes of Canada, 2001, is to be read in accordance with the following as a result of the division on October 2, 2001, of Bill C-15, introduced in the 1st session of the 37th Parliament and entitled the Criminal Law Amendment Act, 2001:
-- src:19071 | (a) the reference in subsection 82(1) of the Act to “Bill C-15” refers, with respect to subsections 82(2) and (4) of the Act, to Bill C-15A, which resulted from the division of Bill C-15 and has the same title;
-- src:19072 | (b) the reference in subsection 82(2) of the Act to “section 25 of the other Act” refers to section 16 of Bill C-15A; and
-- src:19073 | (c) the reference in subsection 82(4) of the Act to “section 62 of the other Act” refers to section 52 of Bill C-15A.
@ref 2004, c. 12, s. 22 (src:19069-19073)
DECLARE `2004 c 12 s 22 reference in section 82 of 2001, c. 32` IS ONE OF
    `2004 c 12 s 22 the reference in subsection 82(1) to Bill C-15, as it applies to subsections 82(2) and (4)`   -- (a)
    `2004 c 12 s 22 the reference in subsection 82(2) to section 25 of the other Act`   -- (b)
    `2004 c 12 s 22 the reference in subsection 82(4) to section 62 of the other Act`   -- (c)
    `2004 c 12 s 22 another reference in section 82`

@ref 2004, c. 12, s. 22 (src:19069-19073)
GIVEN reference IS A `2004 c 12 s 22 reference in section 82 of 2001, c. 32`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`2004 c 12 s 22 the reference is read as referring to` MEANS
    CONSIDER reference
    WHEN `2004 c 12 s 22 the reference in subsection 82(1) to Bill C-15, as it applies to subsections 82(2) and (4)` THEN JUST "Bill C-15A, which resulted from the division of Bill C-15 and has the same title"
    WHEN `2004 c 12 s 22 the reference in subsection 82(2) to section 25 of the other Act` THEN JUST "section 16 of Bill C-15A"
    WHEN `2004 c 12 s 22 the reference in subsection 82(4) to section 62 of the other Act` THEN JUST "section 52 of Bill C-15A"
    WHEN `2004 c 12 s 22 another reference in section 82` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is to be read in accordance with the following"

-- 23 For greater certainty, section 82 of 2001, c. 32 is to be read in accordance with (a) and (b).
-- src:19076 | Interpretation of 2001, c. 32, ss. 82(1) and (3)
-- src:19077 | 23 For greater certainty, section 82 of An Act to amend the Criminal Code (organized crime and law enforcement) and to make consequential amendments to other Acts (“the Act”), chapter 32 of the Statutes of Canada, 2001, is to be read in accordance with the following as a result of the division on October 2, 2001, of Bill C-15, introduced in the 1st session of the 37th Parliament and entitled the Criminal Law Amendment Act, 2001, and the division in the Senate on December 3, 2002, of Bill C-10, introduced in the 2nd session of the 37th Parliament and entitled An Act to amend the Criminal Code (cruelty to animals and firearms) and the Firearms Act:
-- src:19078 | (a) the reference in subsection 82(1) of the Act to “Bill C-15” refers, with respect to subsection 82(3) of the Act, to Bill C-10A, which resulted from the division of Bill C-10 and is entitled An Act to amend the Criminal Code (firearms) and the Firearms Act; and
-- src:19079 | (b) the reference in subsection 82(3) of the Act to “section 32 of the other Act” refers to section 8 of Bill C-10A.
@ref 2004, c. 12, s. 23 (src:19076-19079)
DECLARE `2004 c 12 s 23 reference in section 82 of 2001, c. 32` IS ONE OF
    `2004 c 12 s 23 the reference in subsection 82(1) to Bill C-15, as it applies to subsection 82(3)`   -- (a)
    `2004 c 12 s 23 the reference in subsection 82(3) to section 32 of the other Act`   -- (b)
    `2004 c 12 s 23 another reference in section 82`

@ref 2004, c. 12, s. 23 (src:19076-19079)
GIVEN reference IS A `2004 c 12 s 23 reference in section 82 of 2001, c. 32`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`2004 c 12 s 23 the reference is read as referring to` MEANS
    CONSIDER reference
    WHEN `2004 c 12 s 23 the reference in subsection 82(1) to Bill C-15, as it applies to subsection 82(3)` THEN JUST "Bill C-10A, which resulted from the division of Bill C-10 and is entitled An Act to amend the Criminal Code (firearms) and the Firearms Act"
    WHEN `2004 c 12 s 23 the reference in subsection 82(3) to section 32 of the other Act` THEN JUST "section 8 of Bill C-10A"
    WHEN `2004 c 12 s 23 another reference in section 82` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is to be read in accordance with the following"

§ `2009, c. 29, s. 5 -- Application: persons charged after coming into force`

-- 2009 c 29 s 5: "apply only" -- on or after the day (strictly after, where the text says "after") is within the limit (JUST TRUE); before it, the text says no (JUST FALSE).
-- src:19092 | Application — persons charged after coming into force
-- src:19093 | 5 Subsections 719(3) to (3.4) of the Act, as enacted by section 3, apply only to persons charged after the day on which those subsections come into force.
@ref 2009, c. 29, s. 5 (src:19092-19093)
GIVEN `the day on which subsections 719(3) to (3.4) of the Act come into force` IS A DATE
      `the day the person was charged` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2009 c 29 s 5 the person is within the limit on subsections 719(3) to (3.4)` MEANS
    IF `the day the person was charged` GREATER THAN `the day on which subsections 719(3) to (3.4) of the Act come into force`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "apply only to persons charged after the day on which those subsections come into force"


§ `2011, c. 2, s. 7 -- Applications under section 745.6 (the faint hope clause) pending, and further applications`

-- (1) Applications made under section 745.6 as it read immediately before the day on which section 3 comes into force and still not finally disposed of on that day are dealt with under the Code as it read immediately before that day.
-- src:19096 | Existing applications
-- src:19097 | 7 (1) Applications that were made under section 745.6 of the Criminal Code as that section read immediately before the day on which section 3 comes into force and are still not finally disposed of on that day are to be dealt with and disposed of in accordance with the provisions of the Criminal Code as they read immediately before that day.
@ref 2011, c. 2, s. 7(1) (src:19096-19097)
GIVEN `the application was made under section 745.6 as that section read immediately before the day on which section 3 of 2011, c. 2 comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is still not finally disposed of on that day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2011 c 2 s 7(1) the application is dealt with and disposed of under the Code as it read immediately before that day` MEANS
    IF `the application was made under section 745.6 as that section read immediately before the day on which section 3 of 2011, c. 2 comes into force`
       AND `the application is still not finally disposed of on that day`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Applications that were made under section 745.6 of the Criminal Code as that section read immediately before the day on which section 3 comes into force and are still not finally disposed of on that day"

-- (2) A person who made such an application and is the subject of a determination under 745.61(4) (as it read before) or a determination or conclusion to which 745.63(8) (as it read before) applies may make an application
-- under 745.6(1) as amended within 180 days after the end of two years after the day of the determination or conclusion.
-- "The end of two years after the day" is read as the anniversary two years on, so the window is the 180 days after that anniversary (fork F1 in NOTES.md).
-- src:19098 | Further applications
-- src:19099 | (2) A person who has made an application referred to in subsection (1) and who is the subject of a determination made under subsection 745.61(4) of the Criminal Code, as that subsection read before the day on which this subsection comes into force, or a determination or conclusion to which subsection 745.63(8) of the Criminal Code, as it read before that day, applies, may make an application under subsection 745.6(1) of the Criminal Code, as amended by subsection 3(1), within 180 days after the end of two years after the day on which the person is the subject of the determination or conclusion.
@ref 2011, c. 2, s. 7(2) (src:19098-19099)
GIVEN `the person made an application referred to in subsection 7(1) of 2011, c. 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the subject of a determination under subsection 745.61(4) as it read before the day on which subsection 7(2) comes into force, or of a determination or conclusion to which subsection 745.63(8) as it read before that day applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the person is the subject of the determination or conclusion` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the person makes an application under subsection 745.6(1) as amended by subsection 3(1)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2011 c 2 s 7(2) the person may make an application under subsection 745.6(1) as amended` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person made an application referred to in subsection 7(1) of 2011, c. 2` AND `the person is the subject of a determination under subsection 745.61(4) as it read before the day on which subsection 7(2) comes into force, or of a determination or conclusion to which subsection 745.63(8) as it read before that day applies`)
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who has made an application referred to in subsection (1) and who is the subject of a determination"
        IF `the day on which the person makes an application under subsection 745.6(1) as amended by subsection 3(1)` GREATER THAN `the end of two years after the day of the determination or conclusion`
           AND `the day on which the person makes an application under subsection 745.6(1) as amended by subsection 3(1)` AT MOST (`the end of two years after the day of the determination or conclusion` PLUS 180)
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 180 days after the end of two years after the day on which the person is the subject of the determination or conclusion"
    WHERE
        `the end of two years after the day of the determination or conclusion` MEANS `add years` `the day on which the person is the subject of the determination or conclusion` 2

-- (3) A person who made such an application and in respect of whom a time is set under 745.61(3)(a) or 745.63(6)(a) may make an application under 745.6(1) as amended within 180 days after the end of that time.
-- src:19100 | Further applications
-- src:19101 | (3) A person who has made an application referred to in subsection (1) and in respect of whom a time is set under paragraph 745.61(3)(a) or 745.63(6)(a) of the Criminal Code, as enacted by subsections 4(3) and 5(1), respectively, may make an application under subsection 745.6(1) of the Criminal Code, as amended by subsection 3(1), within 180 days after the end of that time.
@ref 2011, c. 2, s. 7(3) (src:19100-19101)
GIVEN `the person made an application referred to in subsection 7(1) of 2011, c. 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a time is set in respect of the person under paragraph 745.61(3)(a) or 745.63(6)(a) as enacted by subsections 4(3) and 5(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which that time ends` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the person makes an application under subsection 745.6(1) as amended by subsection 3(1)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2011 c 2 s 7(3) the person may make an application under subsection 745.6(1) as amended` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person made an application referred to in subsection 7(1) of 2011, c. 2` AND `a time is set in respect of the person under paragraph 745.61(3)(a) or 745.63(6)(a) as enacted by subsections 4(3) and 5(1)`)
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who has made an application referred to in subsection (1) and in respect of whom a time is set under paragraph 745.61(3)(a) or 745.63(6)(a)"
        IF `the day on which the person makes an application under subsection 745.6(1) as amended by subsection 3(1)` GREATER THAN `the day on which that time ends`
           AND `the day on which the person makes an application under subsection 745.6(1) as amended by subsection 3(1)` AT MOST (`the day on which that time ends` PLUS 180)
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 180 days after the end of that time"

§ `2012, c. 1, ss. 163(a) and 165(b) -- references to a record suspension also refer to a pardon`

-- 163 A reference to an application for a record suspension in the following provisions, as enacted by this Part, is deemed also to be a reference to an application for a pardon that is not finally disposed of
-- on the day on which this section comes into force: (a) paragraph 672.35(c) and subsection 750(4).
-- src:19104 | Pending applications — references in other legislation
-- src:19105 | 163 A reference to an application for a record suspension in the following provisions, as enacted by this Part, is deemed also to be a reference to an application for a pardon that is not finally disposed of on the day on which this section comes into force:
-- src:19106 | (a) paragraph 672.35(c) and subsection 750(4) of the Criminal Code;
@ref 2012, c. 1, par. 163(a) (src:19104-19106)
GIVEN `the provision the reference is in` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the application is an application for a pardon` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is not finally disposed of on the day on which section 163 of 2012, c. 1 comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2012 c 1 s 163(a) the reference to an application for a record suspension is also a reference to an application for a pardon` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the provision the reference is in is paragraph 672.35(c) or subsection 750(4)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the following provisions"
        IF `the application is an application for a pardon` AND `the application is not finally disposed of on the day on which section 163 of 2012, c. 1 comes into force` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an application for a pardon that is not finally disposed of on the day on which this section comes into force"
    WHERE
        `the provision the reference is in is paragraph 672.35(c) or subsection 750(4)` MEANS
                (`the provision the reference is in`'s `section` EQUALS 672.35 AND `the provision the reference is in`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(c)")
            OR  (`the provision the reference is in`'s `section` EQUALS 750 AND `the provision the reference is in`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(4)")

-- 165 A reference to a record suspension in the following provisions, as enacted by this Part, is deemed also to be a reference to a pardon that is granted or issued under the Criminal Records Act: (b) the definition record suspension in subsection 490.011(1).
-- src:19109 | Pardons in effect — references in other legislation
-- src:19110 | 165 A reference to a record suspension in the following provisions, as enacted by this Part, is deemed also to be a reference to a pardon that is granted or issued under the Criminal Records Act:
-- src:19111 | (b) the definition record suspension in subsection 490.011(1) of the Criminal Code;
@ref 2012, c. 1, par. 165(b) (src:19109-19111)
GIVEN `the provision the reference is in` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the reference is in the definition record suspension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the pardon is a pardon that is granted or issued under the Criminal Records Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2012 c 1 s 165(b) the reference to a record suspension is also a reference to a pardon` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the provision the reference is in`'s `section` EQUALS 490.011 AND `the provision the reference is in`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)" AND `the reference is in the definition record suspension`)
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the following provisions"
        IF `the pardon is a pardon that is granted or issued under the Criminal Records Act` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a pardon that is granted or issued under the Criminal Records Act"

§ `2015, c. 13, ss. 37 to 44 -- transitional provisions: victims, sentencing, restitution, hearings`

-- 2015 c 13 s 37: a continuing application for a hearing on the day itself or within 14 days after it. Inside the period JUST TRUE; outside it the text's own period says no (JUST FALSE, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)); a hearing the subsection does not refer to is outside the grant (NOTHING).
-- src:19126 | Hearing — subsection 278.3(5)
-- src:19127 | 37 Subsection 278.3(5) of the Act, as that subsection read immediately before the day on which section 6 of this Act comes into force, continues to apply in respect of any hearing referred to in that subsection that takes place on that day or within 14 days after that day.
@ref 2015, c. 13, s. 37 (src:19126-19127)
GIVEN `the day on which section 6 of 2015, c. 13 comes into force` IS A DATE
      `the day the hearing takes place` IS A DATE
      `the hearing is a hearing referred to in subsection 278.3(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2015 c 13 s 37 subsection 278.3(5) as it read immediately before that day continues to apply to the hearing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the hearing is a hearing referred to in subsection 278.3(5)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any hearing referred to in that subsection"
        IF `the day the hearing takes place` AT LEAST `the day on which section 6 of 2015, c. 13 comes into force` AND `the day the hearing takes place` AT MOST (`the day on which section 6 of 2015, c. 13 comes into force` PLUS 14) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "takes place on that day or within 14 days after that day"


-- 2015 c 13 s 38: "continues to apply" to what was made before the day: before the day is JUST TRUE; any other case is outside the grant's own wording (NOTHING).
-- src:19130 | Restitution requests — section 380.3
-- src:19131 | 38 Section 380.3 of the Act, as that section read immediately before the day on which section 11 of this Act comes into force, continues to apply in respect of requests for restitution made to the court under that section 380.3 before that day.
@ref 2015, c. 13, s. 38 (src:19130-19131)
GIVEN `the day on which section 11 of 2015, c. 13 comes into force` IS A DATE
      `the day the request for restitution was made to the court under section 380.3` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2015 c 13 s 38 section 380.3 as it read immediately before that day continues to apply to the request for restitution` MEANS
    IF `the day the request for restitution was made to the court under section 380.3` LESS THAN `the day on which section 11 of 2015, c. 13 comes into force`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "requests for restitution made to the court under that section 380.3 before that day"


-- 2015 c 13 s 39: "continues to apply" to what was made before the day: before the day is JUST TRUE; any other case is outside the grant's own wording (NOTHING).
