§ `2015, c. 20, s. 28 -- information under subsection 810.01(1) deemed laid under subsection 810.011(1)`

-- 28 If an information has been laid under 810.01(1) before the day this section comes into force by a person who fears on reasonable grounds that another person will commit a terrorism offence and a provincial court judge
-- has not made a final determination with respect to the information, the information is deemed, on that day, to have been laid under 810.011(1). A failed "if" is the text's no within the provision (marginal reading, NOTES.md).
-- src:19162 | Information — terrorism offence
-- src:19163 | 28 If an information has been laid under subsection 810.01(1) of the Criminal Code before the day on which this section comes into force by a person who fears on reasonable grounds that another person will commit a terrorism offence and a provincial court judge has not made a final determination with respect to the information, the information is deemed, on that day, to have been laid under subsection 810.011(1) of that Act.
@ref 2015, c. 20, s. 28 (src:19162-19163)
GIVEN `the information was laid under subsection 810.01(1) before the day on which section 28 of 2015, c. 20 comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information was laid by a person who fears on reasonable grounds that another person will commit a terrorism offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a provincial court judge has not made a final determination with respect to the information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2015 c 20 s 28 the information is deemed to have been laid under subsection 810.011(1)` MEANS
    IF `the information was laid under subsection 810.01(1) before the day on which section 28 of 2015, c. 20 comes into force`
       AND `the information was laid by a person who fears on reasonable grounds that another person will commit a terrorism offence`
       AND `a provincial court judge has not made a final determination with respect to the information`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an information has been laid under subsection 810.01(1) of the Criminal Code before the day on which this section comes into force"
